{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "041K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX' \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\ar[d] \\\\\nZ' \\ar[r] & Z\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$Z' \\to Z$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to Z'$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0006": "$|X'| \\subset |Z'|$", "MATH_0007": "$U' \\subset Z'$", "MATH_0008": "$X'$", "MATH_0009": "$\\text{pr}_0^{-1}(U') = \\text{pr}_1^{-1}(U')$", "MATH_0010": "$Z' \\times_Z Z'$", "MATH_0011": "$U \\subset Z$", "MATH_0012": "$X' = (Z' \\to Z)^{-1}(U)$", "MATH_0013": "$X$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{U' \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0015": "$U' \\to X' \\to X \\in \\check{H}^0(\\mathcal{U}, X)$", "MATH_0016": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0017": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nU' \\ar[r] \\ar[d]^{\\cong} \\ar@/_3ex/[dd] & U \\ar[d] \\ar@/^3ex/[dd] \\\\\nX' \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\ar[d] \\\\\nZ' \\ar[r] & Z\n}\n$$", "MATH_0018": "$T$", "MATH_0019": "$S$", "MATH_0020": "$T$", "MATH_0021": "$T \\to X$", "MATH_0022": "$T \\to X \\to Z$", "MATH_0023": "$Z' \\times_Z T \\to Z'$", "MATH_0024": "$U'$", "MATH_0025": "$T \\to Z$", "MATH_0026": "$U$", "MATH_0027": "$U \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-closed-immersion-local}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{descent-lemma-open-fpqc-covering}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-properties-proposition-sheaf-fpqc}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:50b818bc091a81b7d2298295a77a84155e83642b95e82d0c4cbcc5b91c950eb3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:193f55e6c244367d87f7e616fab0a4862be65074e1339444730dfc3af4c547d4", "source_text": "We will use\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto prove this. Assumptions (1) and (2) of that lemma follow from\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nConsider a cartesian diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof algebraic spaces over <MATH_0002>\nwhere <MATH_0003> is a surjective flat morphism of affine schemes,\nand <MATH_0004> is an open immersion. We have to show that <MATH_0005>\nis an open immersion. Note that <MATH_0006> corresponds to an\nopen subscheme <MATH_0007> (isomorphic to <MATH_0008>)\nwith the property that <MATH_0009>\nas open subschemes of <MATH_0010>. Hence there exists an open\nsubscheme <MATH_0011> such that <MATH_0012>, see\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nBy Properties of Spaces,\nProposition <REF_0004>\nwe see that <MATH_0013> satisfies the sheaf condition for the fpqc topology.\nNow we have the fpqc covering <MATH_0014>\nand the element <MATH_0015>.\nBy the sheaf condition we obtain a morphism <MATH_0016> such that\n<MATH_0017>\nis commutative. On the other hand, we know that for any scheme <MATH_0018> over <MATH_0019>\nand <MATH_0020>-valued point <MATH_0021> the composition <MATH_0022> is a\nmorphism such that <MATH_0023> factors through <MATH_0024>. Clearly\nthis means that <MATH_0025> factors through <MATH_0026>. In other words the map\nof sheaves <MATH_0027> is bijective and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:023b5120b81002ee28d302a0f0203fa06b1c7e7ba7a8af2c49d43dd44abbf486", "unit_id": "tag:041X:proof"}
